{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart@navapbc.com","data":{"body":"CONTAMINATION TRANSFER TEST - negative. With two CE runs on the same plan, one from the contaminated tree with a full 6-of-6 persona team and one from the cleaned tree with 5 of 6, the question of whether any arm consumed rebar's leaked cache became directly testable. Lexical best-match overlap of each CE finding against rebar's 15 findings: contaminated run mean 0.090 with a single item above 0.25 (at 0.254), clean run mean 0.076 with none above 0.25. The difference is inside normal run-to-run and team-size variation, so there is no evidence of transfer. DECISION: score the contaminated-tree run, because it has proven full persona coverage and a tested-negative contamination risk, while the clean run has a PROVEN coverage defect; a proven defect outweighs a tested-for and undetected risk. The clean run is preserved as a persona-degraded control. This decision is recorded for override rather than buried."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789443903794812001,"uuid":"b107d20c-aab0-4dc9-86e3-b66cb4671cd1"}